From: Realme X2 Pro Linux port <hmhmdcy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] scripts: activate NCM only when carrier is present

usb-signaller creates the NCM profile as soon as the gadget is bound.  A
gadget bound to a UDC exists before the USB host has enumerated it, so
usb0 can exist with carrier 0.  Calling nmcli connection up at that point
forces NetworkManager to report an active wired connection even though
there is no USB link.  On Plasma Mobile this leaves a permanent wired
network indicator in the status bar.

Keep the profile's autoconnect enabled, but only request an explicit
activation when the kernel reports carrier 1.  NetworkManager then
activates the profile when a host actually raises carrier and deactivates
it when the cable is removed.  The same rule applies to Developer and
Tethering NCM modes.

diff --git a/distro/scripts/usb-signaller-developer-mode.sh b/distro/scripts/usb-signaller-developer-mode.sh
--- a/distro/scripts/usb-signaller-developer-mode.sh
+++ b/distro/scripts/usb-signaller-developer-mode.sh
@@ -69,6 +69,10 @@ activate_connection() {
     return 1
 }
 
+carrier_is_up() {
+    [ "$(cat "/sys/class/net/$IFACE/carrier" 2>/dev/null)" = 1 ]
+}
+
 up() {
     # The host can take a moment to create the NCM netdev and raise carrier
     # after a gadget rebind. Do not make the mode service fail prematurely.
@@ -82,10 +86,12 @@ up() {
     # Bring interface and NetworkManager connection up without saving connection
     nmcli connection add con-name "$CONNECTION_NAME" type ethernet \
         ifname "$IFACE" ipv4.method manual ipv4.addresses "$IP_ADDRESS_SERVER"/16 \
-	save no >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
-    if [ -e "/sys/class/net/$IFACE" ]; then
+	autoconnect yes save no >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
+    if carrier_is_up; then
         activate_connection ||
             echo "NetworkManager will retry when $IFACE is ready"
+    else
+        echo "NetworkManager will activate $IFACE when carrier appears"
     fi
 
     # Start DHCP server
diff --git a/distro/scripts/usb-signaller-tethering-mode.sh b/distro/scripts/usb-signaller-tethering-mode.sh
--- a/distro/scripts/usb-signaller-tethering-mode.sh
+++ b/distro/scripts/usb-signaller-tethering-mode.sh
@@ -45,6 +45,10 @@ activate_connection() {
     return 1
 }
 
+carrier_is_up() {
+    [ "$(cat "/sys/class/net/$IFACE/carrier" 2>/dev/null)" = 1 ]
+}
+
 up() {
     # The host can take a moment to create the NCM netdev and raise carrier
     # after a gadget rebind. Do not make the mode service fail prematurely.
@@ -57,10 +61,12 @@ up() {
 
     # Bring interface and NetworkManager connection up without saving connection
     nmcli connection add con-name "$CONNECTION_NAME" type ethernet \
-        ifname "$IFACE" ipv4.method shared save no >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
-    if [ -e "/sys/class/net/$IFACE" ]; then
+        ifname "$IFACE" ipv4.method shared autoconnect yes save no >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
+    if carrier_is_up; then
         activate_connection ||
             echo "NetworkManager will retry when $IFACE is ready"
+    else
+        echo "NetworkManager will activate $IFACE when carrier appears"
     fi
  
     # NetworkManager does not always turn IP forwarding ON, set it manually to be sure
